Why does he ask the question?

cue0109157
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.000
He says, I don't know the answer.

cue0109158
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.000
He should give the answer

cue0109159
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.000
or he doesn't ask the question.

cue0109160
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.000
He says, by the faith of Rashid, ask the question.

cue0109161
00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.000
And he says, I don't know.

cue0109162
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.000
He's inviting all those to think about it.

cue0109163
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.000
Other people to think about it.

cue0109164
00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.000
Maybe other people will figure out an answer.

cue0109165
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.000
He says, I know the answer.

cue0109166
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.000
What is the answer?

cue0109167
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.000
According to Jewish law,

cue0109168
00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:08.000
what determines whether a child is first born or not?

cue0109169
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Not the father.

cue0109170
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.000
Not the father.

cue0109171
00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.000
But exclusively the mother.

cue0109172
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.000
Only the mother.

cue0109173
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.000
You know the law?

cue0109174
00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.000
That's only the mother.

cue0109175
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.000
Not the father.

cue0109176
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.000
And look what the Basuk says.

cue0109177
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.000
Who is brought first?

cue0109178
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.000
Yaʿaqoḇ.

cue0109179
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.000
Yaʿaqoḇ.

cue0109180
00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.000
By the fact that they brought first Yaʿaqoḇ means

cue0109181
00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:33.000
now the Tora recognizes Yaʿaqoḇ as the actual begor.

cue0109182
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.000
And this is the lesson that we learn from Yaʿaqoḇ.

cue0109183
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.000
That's the history of Israel.

cue0109184
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.000
That namely,

cue0109185
00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.000
although there was a natural impossibility

cue0109186
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.000
for Yaʿaqoḇ to be the firstborn,

cue0109187
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.000
he fought against this natural impossibility

cue0109188
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.000
and he won.

cue0109189
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.000
And this is the history of the Jewish people.

cue0109190
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.000
There are natural odds

cue0109191
00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.000
against us becoming the firstborn of the nations.

cue0109192
00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.000
Everything from a natural point of view

cue0109193
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.000
is against us.

cue0109194
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.000
But we are stubborn.

cue0109195
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.000
We persevere.

cue0109196
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.000
We fight.

cue0109197
00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.000
We don't give up.

cue0109198
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.000
And at the end,

cue0109199
00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.000
Yiṣḥaq recognizes us.

cue0109200
00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.000
Rekha recognizes us.

cue0109201
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.000
Even Esau recognizes us.

cue0109202
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.000
And finally,

cue0109203
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.000
like here in the next Tora Sha'ar

cue0109204
00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.000
that we study today in the Mincha,

cue0109205
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.000
we learn today from Mincha,

cue0109206
00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.000
God reveals himself to Yaʿaqoḇ

cue0109207
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:23.000
and recognizes Yaʿaqoḇ as his begor.

cue0109208
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.000
Although it's against nature.

cue0109209
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.000
Of course it's against nature.

cue0109210
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.000
I'm not answering your question.

cue0109211
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.000
I beg your pardon?

cue0109212
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.000
Of course.

cue0109213
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.000
Afterwards.

cue0109214
00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.000
Because when I said it's not.

cue0109215
00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.000
He tricked me twice.

cue0109216
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.000
He tricked me twice.

cue0109217
00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.000
Once before when I told you.

cue0109218
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.000
He didn't know Esau.

cue0109219
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.000
He's half, of course.

cue0109220
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.000
He didn't know.

cue0109221
00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.000
Just one...

cue0109222
00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.000
One question.

cue0109223
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.000
I just want to make an observation.

cue0109224
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.000
I once read an explanation

cue0109225
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.000
that Jacob was conceived first.

cue0109226
00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.000
But that's true.

cue0109227
00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.000
But according to Jewish law.

cue0109228
00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.000
What is...

cue0109229
00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.000
Who is a begor?

cue0109230
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.000
You can twist it any way you want.

cue0109231
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.000
But you see,

cue0109232
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.000
twist it any way you want.

cue0109233
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.000
If a woman today has two children,

cue0109234
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.000
who is the begor?

cue0109235
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.000
Esau.

cue0109236
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.000
Of course.

cue0109237
00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.000
From a natural point of view,

cue0109238
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.000
twist it any way you want.

cue0109239
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.000
Esau is the begor.

cue0109240
00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.000
But nonetheless,

cue0109241
00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:24.000
this is the lesson that we learn from Yaʿaqoḇ.

cue0109242
00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.000
We do not have to accept even the natural best.

cue0109243
00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.000
Still the Jewish people have the power

cue0109244
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.000
to fight over and to change things.

cue0109245
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.000
That is the truth.

cue0109246
00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.000
That's what we learn from Yaʿaqoḇ.

cue0109247
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.000
One, two, three, testing.

cue0109248
00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.000
One, two, three, testing.

cue0109249
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.000
One, two, three.

cue0109250
00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.000
I say go.

cue0109251
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.000
Go ahead.

cue0109252
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:40.000
The End
